The five limbo-*.json files are a subset of x509-limbo's limbo.json, made by jq from the file
of the commit below (docs/design/tls.md, item 10): every case not of the family bettertls, and
the cases of bettertls in file order while the cases kept, each as compact JSON, sum to at most
20 MiB (20,971,520 bytes). The subset is split by case group so that no test reads it whole:
limbo-other.json holds 234 cases of the other families, limbo-bettertls-1.json to -4.json
the kept cases of bettertls (all of them bettertls::nameconstraints) in four runs of file
order, 1,228, 1,228, 1,228 and 1,225 cases. Each file is {"version":1,"testcases":[...]}, the
cases in file order, written as compact JSON. LICENSE is copied unchanged. parse-counts.txt is
written by the tests limbo_parse of surf-tls, not by x509-limbo.

dropped: the field peer_certificate_key of every kept case, after the cases are chosen. It holds
the peer's private key as PEM (216 values, all in limbo-other.json; null in every bettertls
case) and is the only field of a case that holds a private key. surf's tests read the
certificates, trust anchors and expected results; none uses a peer's private key (the test
server takes its keys from crates/tls-test-certs). Dropping it keeps private keys out of the
repository. Every other field is kept unchanged.

left out after the cases are chosen: the case online::facebook.com (SUCCESS, SERVER, 3
certificates). A secret scanner's token pattern (gitleaks square-access-token) matches a run of
the leaf certificate's base64; the certificate is public and holds no token.

